# Types

Silent on untyped files (Bash, JSON, CSS, Markdown). On typed files: fix the design, do not silence the compiler.

- No TS `any` (Go `any` differs).
- `unknown` may stay unvalidated until checked. Passing `unknown` to a validator or an explicitly untrusted container is legitimate. Narrow or validate before trusted domain use.
- No blind casts or ignored errors; unwrap only in tests or proven invariants.
- Do not add suppressions just to pass CI (`@ts-ignore`, `# type: ignore` without a one-line why). Interop exceptions must be narrow, documented, and repo-consistent.
- Prefer sum types over parallel booleans; the repo's fallible-op idiom; explicit public signatures; schema-inferred types when schemas exist; one nullish convention per repo.

An escape hatch is a design bug.
